      }
    },
    {
      "name": "nonveg_main_daily_pair",
      "type": "slot_composition",
      "base_slot": "nonveg_main",
      "min_slot_count": 2,
      "max_slot_count": 4,
      "components": [
        {
          "selector": {
            "flag": "is_nonveg_dry"
          },
          "count": 1
        },
        {
          "selector": {
            "any_flag": [
              "is_north_chicken_gravy",
              "is_south_chicken_gravy"
            ]
          },
          "count": 1
        }
      ],
      "components_by_theme": {
        "chinese": [
          {
            "selector": {
              "cuisine_family": "chinese"
            },
            "count": 1
          },
          {
            "selector": {
              "any_flag": [
                "is_north_chicken_gravy",
                "is_south_chicken_gravy"
              ]
            },
            "count": 1
          }
        ],
        "biryani": [
          {
            "selector": {
              "flag": "is_nonveg_biryani"
            },
            "count": 1
          },
          {
            "selector": {
              "any_flag": [
                "is_north_chicken_gravy",
                "is_south_chicken_gravy"
              ]
            },
            "count": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "_comment": "A 5-dish non-veg lunch station: biryani + chicken gravy + chicken dry + kebab + egg, every day. Gated to counters configured with 5 nonveg_main so it is inert elsewhere, and nonveg_main_daily_pair is capped at 4 so the two never compose the same counter. The five components must land on five DISTINCT dishes, and because the components are >= bounds one dish satisfying two of them frees a cell for a duplicate: the kebab (tandoori_murgh_lababdar) also carries is_nonveg_gravy, and egg curries carry it too, so the station came back with two eggs and no chicken gravy. The gravy and dry components therefore exclude both egg and the tandoor flags, leaving each component one role only. L&T's printed menu has separate 'Non Veg Gravey', 'Non VEG Dry', 'Chicken Kabab' and 'Egg Items' rows, which is exactly this shape.",
      "name": "nonveg_main_five_dish",
      "type": "slot_composition",
      "base_slot": "nonveg_main",
      "min_slot_count": 5,
      "components": [
        {
          "selector": {
            "flag": "is_nonveg_biryani"
          },
          "count": 1
        },
        {
          "selector": {
            "flag": "is_nonveg_gravy"
          },
          "exclude": {
            "any_flag": [
              "is_egg_dish",
              "is_tandoor",
              "is_tandoor_nonveg_dry"
            ]
          },
          "count": 1
        },
        {
          "selector": {
            "flag": "is_nonveg_dry"
          },
          "exclude": {
            "any_flag": [
              "is_egg_dish",
              "is_tandoor",
              "is_tandoor_nonveg_dry"
            ]
          },
          "count": 1
        },
        {
          "selector": {
            "any_flag": [
              "is_tandoor",
              "is_tandoor_nonveg_dry"
            ]
          },
          "count": 1
        },
        {
          "selector": {
            "flag": "is_egg_dish"
          },
          "count": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "veg_dry_north_south_pair",
      "type": "slot_composition",
      "base_slot": "veg_dry",
      "min_slot_count": 2,
      "components": [
        {
          "selector": {
            "cuisine_family": "north_indian"
          },
          "count": 1
        },
        {
          "selector": {
            "cuisine_family": "south_indian"
          },
          "count": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_comment": "Paneer belongs on a mix / south / north day; chinese and biryani days are the fallback, not the default (client rule, all cities). SOFT on purpose: the hard equivalent is selector_frequency.allowed_day_types, which forbids paneer on the other days outright — and a counter themed chinese or biryani every weekday would then never serve paneer at all. `holiday` (a weekend day on a serve_weekends counter) is not in the preferred list either, so paneer lands on a working day.",
      "name": "paneer_prefers_mix_south_north_days",
      "type": "soft_preference",
      "mode": "prefer_day_types",
      "priority": "high",
      "selector": {
        "key_ingredient": "paneer"
      },
      "day_types": [
        "mix",
        "south",
        "north"
      ]
    },
    {
      "_comment": "No soya, baby corn, chole or mushroom on a paneer day (client rule, all cities) — they read as substitutes for each other, so serving two wastes a slot. Counted across every slot because the point is the day's plate: a paneer gravy next to a soya veg dry is exactly the pairing to avoid. 'chole' is selected as the chana-gravy family (is_chana_gravy) since that is how the ontology files chole in both cities; the flag also covers the other whole-legume gravies, which fits the intent. Pune carries no mushroom dish, so that part of the selector is simply inert there. Baby corn is matched on the NAME, not on key_ingredient: that column tags 67 Bangalore rows baby_corn of which only 3 are baby-corn dishes (it is the de-facto default for a mixed salad, incl. iceberg_lettuce and black_olives) while the 34 dishes actually named after baby corn are tagged corn / bell_pepper / cauliflower. A HARD rule on that column would ban nearly every salad from paneer days and still miss 31 of the 34 real dishes. A dish matching BOTH sides (chole_paneer) counts as paneer only \u2014 see SameDayExclusionRule._hits.",
      "name": "paneer_not_with_soya_babycorn_chole_mushroom",
      "type": "same_day_exclusion",
      "selector": {
        "key_ingredient": "paneer"
      },
      "exclude": {
        "any_of": [
          {
            "key_ingredient": "soy"
          },
          {
            "name_contains": [
              "babycorn",
              "baby_corn"
            ]
          },
          {
            "flag": "is_chana_gravy"
          },
          {
            "key_ingredient": "mushroom"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
